11. SCD TYPE 1 - CUSTOMERS

SCD Type 1 means history is NOT maintained.

SQL:
TRUNCATE TABLE edwdb_chandb.dim_customers;

Then:
INSERT INTO edwdb_chandb.dim_customers (
    CustomerID,
    FirstName,
    LastName,
    Email,
    PhoneNumber,
    Address,
    DateOfBirth,
    BranchID,
    effective_date
)
SELECT DISTINCT
    CustomerID,
    FirstName,
    LastName,
    Email,
    PhoneNumber,
    Address,
    DateOfBirth,
    BranchID,
    CURRENT_DATE
FROM odsdb_chandb.ods_cust_profile;

The TRUNCATE removes all existing customer records.

The INSERT reloads the latest customer data.

Example:
Before:
CustomerID = 101
Address = Chennai

Customer changes address to Bangalore.

After Type 1:
CustomerID = 101
Address = Bangalore

The old Chennai value is gone.

This is effectively a FULL REFRESH Type 1 implementation.

CUSTOMER DIMENSION COLUMNS:
CustomerID
FirstName
LastName
Email
PhoneNumber
Address
DateOfBirth
BranchID
effective_date

ONE-LINE SUMMARY:
Customer dimension uses SCD Type 1, so only the latest customer information is retained and previous values are not preserved.


12. SCD TYPE 2 - BRANCHES

SCD Type 2 means historical changes ARE maintained.

Example:

Day 1:
BranchID = 10
BranchName = Chennai Branch
City = Chennai
is_current = 1

Later branch changes city.

Old record:
BranchID = 10
City = Chennai
end_date = 2026-09-02
is_current = 0

New record:
BranchID = 10
City = Bangalore
start_date = 2026-09-03
end_date = NULL
is_current = 1

History is preserved.


13. SCD TYPE 2 UPDATE

SQL:
UPDATE edwdb_chandb.dim_branches d
JOIN odsdb_chandb.ods_branches o
  ON d.BranchID = o.BranchID
SET d.end_date = CURRENT_DATE - INTERVAL 1 DAY,
    d.is_current = 0
WHERE d.is_current = 1
  AND d.BranchID IS NOT NULL
  AND (d.Address <> o.Address
    OR d.BranchName <> o.BranchName
    OR d.City <> o.City
    OR d.State <> o.State
    OR d.Zipcode <> o.Zipcode);

The query finds the current branch using:
d.is_current = 1

It compares old EDW data against new ODS data.

Compared columns:
Address
BranchName
City
State
Zipcode

If any value changed:
old record -> expired

It sets:
is_current = 0
end_date = yesterday

Why yesterday?

If today is 2026-09-03:
CURRENT_DATE - INTERVAL 1 DAY = 2026-09-02

So the old record is valid until yesterday.


14. SCD TYPE 2 INSERT

SQL:
INSERT INTO edwdb_chandb.dim_branches (
    Address,
    BranchID,
    BranchName,
    City,
    State,
    Zipcode,
    start_date,
    end_date,
    is_current
)
SELECT
    o.Address,
    o.BranchID,
    o.BranchName,
    o.City,
    o.State,
    o.Zipcode,
    CURRENT_DATE,
    NULL,
    1
FROM odsdb_chandb.ods_branches o
LEFT JOIN edwdb_chandb.dim_branches d
       ON o.BranchID = d.BranchID
      AND d.is_current = 1
WHERE d.BranchID IS NULL
   OR d.Address <> o.Address
   OR d.BranchName <> o.BranchName
   OR d.City <> o.City
   OR d.State <> o.State
   OR d.Zipcode <> o.Zipcode;

This handles:
1. New branch
2. Existing branch with changed attributes

New/current record gets:
start_date = CURRENT_DATE
end_date = NULL
is_current = 1

SCD TYPE 2 COLUMNS:
BranchID
BranchName
Address
City
State
Zipcode
start_date
end_date
is_current

ONE-LINE SUMMARY:
Branch dimension uses SCD Type 2 by expiring changed records and inserting a new current version while preserving historical records.


