17. EDW FACT LOAN LOAD

FLOW:
ODS Loans
   |
   +-- Customer lookup
   |
   +-- Branch lookup
           |
           v
       fact_loans

SQL:
INSERT INTO edwdb_chandb.fact_loans (
    LoanID,
    CustomerID,
    BranchID,
    Amount,
    InterestRate,
    StartDate,
    EndDate,
    PaymentFrequency,
    Status,
    OutstandingBalance,
    LoanDurationMonths,
    RiskIndicator,
    HighValueFlag,
    load_dt,
    load_ts
)
SELECT DISTINCT
    o.LoanID,
    c.CustomerID,
    b.BranchID,
    o.Amount,
    o.InterestRate,
    o.StartDate,
    o.EndDate,
    o.PaymentFrequency,
    o.Status,
    o.Amount AS OutstandingBalance,
    TIMESTAMPDIFF(MONTH, o.StartDate, o.EndDate) AS LoanDurationMonths,
    CASE
        WHEN o.InterestRate > 12 THEN 'HIGH'
        WHEN o.InterestRate BETWEEN 8 AND 12 THEN 'MEDIUM'
        ELSE 'LOW'
    END AS RiskIndicator,
    CASE
        WHEN o.Amount >= 1000000 THEN 'Y'
        ELSE 'N'
    END AS HighValueFlag,
    CURRENT_DATE,
    CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
FROM odsdb_chandb.ods_loans o
LEFT JOIN edwdb_chandb.dim_customers c
    ON o.CustomerID = c.CustomerID
LEFT JOIN edwdb_chandb.dim_branches b
    ON c.BranchID = b.BranchID
   AND b.is_current = 1;

Why joins?

Loan contains CustomerID.

Customer dimension gives Customer -> Branch relationship.

Branch dimension gives branch information.

Flow:
Loan -> Customer -> Branch


